# Setup

## 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/cansathandler/UNAGI-
cd UNAGI-
```

---

## 2. Create a virtual environment

### Linux / macOS

```bash
python3 -m venv unagi_env
```

### Windows

```powershell
python -m venv unagi_env
```

---

## 3. Activate the virtual environment

### Linux / macOS

```bash
source unagi_env/bin/activate
```

### Windows (PowerShell)

```powershell
unagi_env\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

### Windows (Command Prompt)

```cmd
unagi_env\Scripts\activate.bat
```

---

## 4. Install the project dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## 5. Verify the installation

```bash
python -c "import cv2; print(cv2.__version__)"
```

Verify that AprilTag support is available:

```bash
python -c "import cv2; print(hasattr(cv2.aruco, 'DICT_APRILTAG_36h11'))"
```

Expected output:

```text
True
```

---

## 6. Generate a sample AprilTag

```bash
python generate_apriltag.py
```

This creates:

```
tags/
└── tag_0.png
```

---

## 7. Run the tracker

```bash
python apriltag_tracker.py
```